+## Managed file protocol
+
+The Unix-only `downloads managed` command is intended for a trusted local
+application, not an Internet-facing service. All JSON files are atomically
+replaced. Store directories use mode 0700 and files 0600. Authentication and music
+must never be included in an application package or public status.
+
+Each sync carries `--request ID` (before the action). Its job status contains
+`version`, `request`, `account_id`, `uri`, `phase`, `completed`, `total`, `bytes`,
+public `tracks`, `error` and private process identity. Consumers must reject old
+request IDs and account mismatches. Phases are resolving/downloading/verifying,
+then complete/error; a recovered dead job becomes interrupted. A stable lock
+prevents concurrent writers. Sync while the offline player is active is allowed
+only when playback is paused.
+
+The store contains account-specific pending downloads and immutable generations.
+An atomic index plus backup selects complete snapshots; playlist order and the
+Spotify snapshot ID are checked before publication. Quota/free-space checks count
+actual audio sizes and preserve a safety reserve. Account changes invalidate the
+old catalog; forget stops only owned jobs and deletes this backend's credentials.
+
+Playback takes a numeric/hyphen session ID, a zero-based initial index and optional
+resume. The command file is `{ "session": "1000-2", "commands": [
+{ "id": 1, "action": "pause" }, { "id": 2, "action": "seek", "value": 5000 } ] }`.
+IDs increase monotonically; the status `ack` lets the application remove processed
+commands. Supported actions: pause, resume, next, prev, seek (milliseconds), skip
+(seconds), stop. The application caps the queue at 32.
+Status includes version, session, phase, index, position_ms, ack, error and process
+identity. Controls for another session are ignored. The integrating application
+owns volume, parent permissions and routing from physical figures/buttons.
